      "raw_local_commit_utf8": "tree 34f835a6f9bded04e5ab943a23ffb9e07904e1dc\nparent 20e026f5e5bffc6ea044f6216b28f66cfaa1b156\nauthor Codex <codex@openai.com> 1794989151 -0700\ncommitter Codex <codex@openai.com> 1794989151 -0700\n\nImplement managed native matmul and runtime lifetime safety\n\nAdd the P03-T02 internal managed operator for the six frozen FP16/BF16\nmatmul signatures, a matching 56-byte device reader and ordinary WMMA\nkernel, strict compiler-record binding, and a bounded SimX/native-RTL\nqualification runner with independent exact-bit fixtures.\n\nKeep queued buffers, kernels, events, module setup and transfer staging\nowned through completion and failure. Retire a synchronous software CP\ncopy after a host exception so released staging cannot be replayed.\nSuccessful CP tick ordering is unchanged. Add host fault-injection and\nactual-runtime bounds, lifetime, allocation and transfer recovery tests.\n\nExpand governance source filters and select the existing runtime smoke\ncase for SimX on RV32/RV64. The runtime catalog change increases selected\ncoverage; no tolerance, golden, installed API, RTL or toolchain pin changes.\nPreserve historical A01 source bodies and acceptance provenance.\n\nReviewed independently by execution_review, runtime_review,\nfailure_path_review and integration_audit with disjoint ownership;\nauthor fixes received a second reviewer. User authorized implementation,\ncommit and push to master. No waiver or human review is fabricated.\n\nValidation before freeze: 45 focused host tests, project governance,\nreal RV64 SimX matmul smoke, 12 actual lifecycle groups and diff checks.\nFormal complete matrix and phase acceptance remain pending this commit.\n",
