      "raw_local_commit_utf8": "tree 6de56163cd0bfcc63ffc0de7bc2c9fff44627c80\nparent 319ad63532cee17ae88fa75757a5ac87ed5c6a77\nauthor Codex <codex@openai.com> 1794991274 -0700\ncommitter Codex <codex@openai.com> 1794991274 -0700\n\nAccept P03 managed operators after native execution qualification\n\nClose P03-A02/A03 and P03-T02 for the six declared FP16/BF16 matmul\nsignatures, preserving the historical A01 contract and unsupported\noperator families. Next is P04-T01's model/fixture freeze; P01-A03 vendor\nhw_emu remains blocked and required before P07.\n\nClean implementation 319ad63532cee17ae88fa75757a5ac87ed5c6a77 passed:\n- 210 bounded matrix commands, 176 case executions and 352 actual launches\n- on SimX/native processor RTL, with 14,336 exact output-word comparisons;\n- all 1,669 host tests, including 45 P03 checks, no failures/errors/skips;\n- 12 actual lifecycle groups in each RV64 p02-tfr and default RV32 SimX.\n\nRetain exact logs, compiler roles, wire/dispatch records, source/tool and\nartifact hashes, independent reviews, and earlier failures/interruptions\nin compact archives. Independent qualification reconstructs the raw\ncomparisons without using the new output parser. Final delivery review\nverifies 632 archive members and source identity. Code, tests and CI are\nunchanged from the tested implementation; manifest change is next-action\nprose only.\n\nUpdate canonical phase gates, status, contract, handoff and backlog.\nKeep timeout ownership, trusted build binding, simulated failure scope,\npartial-DMA and physical-hardware limits explicit. No goldens, bounds,\ninstalled interfaces or protected assets change. Original user authorized\nimplementation, commit and direct master publication; no waiver or human\nreview is fabricated.\n",
